			"date": "2026-02-18T06:34:29.525Z",
			"content": "<p>The contrarian standpoint here would be \"evolution\":</p>\n<p>The biological process really does not care how things get build or how things work and still is able to produce most interesting species.</p>\n<p>Of course this comes at the price of constant churn (hunting and eating each other) and is extremely slow.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:web:fry69.dev/app.bsky.feed.post/3mf4hkpqi7k2s",
			"parentId": "at://did:web:fry69.dev/app.bsky.feed.post/3mf4hkp73l22s",
